    {
      "id": "1978a921-c78f-4aef-949d-f27868cf4cf1",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-30T19:58:17.000Z",
      "title": "Dividend of ₹20.00 announced",
      "body": "Dividend of ₹20.00 is the same as last year. Ex-date: 4th June 2026 Payment date: 27th June 2026 Dividend yield will be 0.8%, which is higher than the industry average of 0.6%. Sustainability & Growth Dividend is well covered by both earnings (18% earnings payout ratio) and cash flows (34% cash payout ratio). The dividend has increased by an average of 15% per year over the past 10 years. However, payments have been volatile during that time. EPS is expected to grow by 41% over the next 2 years, which should provide support to the dividend and adequate earnings cover.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "f0905afb-60c2-4122-8f1e-11989810ead4",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-29T11:51:24.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS exceeds analyst expectations while revenues lag behind",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹126 (up from ₹112 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹28.6b (up 10% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹2.85b (up 11% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 10.0% (in line with FY 2025). Revenue missed analyst estimates by 1.7%. Earnings per share (EPS) exceeded analyst estimates by 1.5%. Revenue is forecast to grow 10% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, compared to a 12% growth forecast for the Machinery industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 1% per year but the company’s share price has increased by 17% per year, which means it is tracking significantly ahead of earnings growth.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
